id: pm-starter-4kvb
title: Measure agent task cost baselines for extension authors
description: "Reproducible consumer-example baselines for orientation, targeted-read and resume scenarios. Measures tool calls, delivered bytes and elapsed work. Not model performance, not external capture accounting, and not native operation benchmarks."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: audit-1026,cost-baseline
created_at: "2026-10-27T16:56:48.970Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T14:25:32.313Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T14:25:27.737Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T16:11:05.000Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every baseline declares corpus/version and expected answer; repeated runs report distributions; byte/4 estimates are labeled estimates; a deliberate extra full-list call worsens the measured call/byte budget.
release: 2026.10.29
resolution: "Delivered by PR #167 (b8a6d5b): Measure repeatable agent task costs and expose wasted full reads"
expected_result: Every baseline declares corpus/version and expected answer; repeated runs report distributions; byte/4 estimates are labeled estimates; a deliberate extra full-list call worsens the measured call/byte budget.
actual_result: "PR #167 merged at 2026-10-28T16:11:05Z as b8a6d5b; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T16:57:06.330Z",pi-agent,"Overlap check (re-run against the pinned SDK 2026.10.23 and sibling package READMEs before design):\n\n- pm-cli ships an internal release ratchet (docs/agent-task-token-baseline.json plus the agent-task token gate). It replays fixed CLI transcripts and compares ceil(bytes/4) estimates for core protocols. That gate is a core release claim, not a consumer example extension authors can run against their own tracker.\n- pm-observer measures external producer captures (transcript tokens, attribution, continuity). It does not measure SDK tool-call and delivered-byte budgets for fixed orientation, targeted-read and resume scenarios.\n- pm-rust benchmarks native workspace operations. It is not a TypeScript consumer example.\n\nThis item is a reproducible pm-starter example for extension authors. It declares corpus/version and an expected answer, reports distributions over repeated runs, labels byte/4 figures as estimates, and shows that one extra full-list call worsens the measured call and byte budget. It does not claim model performance.\n\nDesign: host-injected SDK only (context orient intent, certified list, get, producer cursors, schemaList roles, workspace transactions). No argv/which/symlink SDK resolution."
  "2026-10-27T17:36:51.493Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: the prior work is uncommitted on the requested branch; no remote feature branch or open PR exists. Reusing this item and its acceptance criteria. Rechecked sibling scope: observer owns external capture attribution; rust owns native-operation benchmarks; the CLI internal task-token ratchet owns its core release protocol. This package supplies a reproducible consumer example. Preserve the read-only scenario measurement, exact budget comparisons and host injection. The speculative baseline-sync mutation surface is not part of the requested task: it currently splits preview/apply decisions, does not use its transaction hook, and cannot prove deletion ownership. Remove that unsafe unshipped surface; baseline declarations are portable JSON values, with no tracker import, sync, journal, lease or compensation path. Test producer/validator round trips and seeded read-back scenarios instead."
  "2026-10-27T17:54:00.500Z",codex-agent,"Targeted SDK evidence: strict schema and numeric-output fuzzing, 500 seeded portable-declaration replay sequences with periodic native SDK read-back, custom registry role checks, real compact continuation pages, eight-page refusal, corpus revision rechecks, exact rational budget boundaries, and native read-contract fault injection. These are read-only declarations: no package import/export/sync mutation paths or shared journal/lease state exist. Found and corrected SDK short-ID resolution and compact continuation-envelope assumptions. Added a packaged CLI integration test after the harness missed Commander camelCase flag keys. Public read-only copy at main revision bef8690 contains 83 items; initial scenario medians are 2/2/3 calls and 5613/1643/6329 UTF-8 JSON bytes, with an extra full-list delta of 1 call and 290014 bytes. Final runtime and packed-install evidence follows."
  "2026-10-27T18:04:25.448Z",codex-agent,"Verified through the linked pm test runner: 10 tests passed, 0 failed, with 100% lines/branches/functions for baselines.ts at unchanged 100% thresholds. Behavioral revert proof ran in a disposable copy: disabling only executeOnce's injected measured listAllComplete call made the regression fail with budget_not_worsened (exit 1); the actual source hash stayed unchanged and the restored implementation passed the full targeted command. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass (102 documented declarations). Public read-only data validation passes on Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5 with identical answers/byte budgets and unchanged hashes. Two corpus observations cost 2 calls / 580028 bytes separately from the scenario budgets. One writable-fixture run truthfully refused a changed orientation answer; the diagnostic trace is retained in the test and the subsequent exact-source linked run passes. No model/network-remote performance claim is made."
  "2026-10-27T18:06:31.018Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed all 5 installation paths using the same package bytes (SHA-256 d01c0e3fb1234ebdc0cdff0260eca231bee083fe3639b37af45c205e24813823): npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx forced to Bun, and project-local. Every path replayed the same three answers, passed the full-list budget probe, and returned a typed exit-2 refusal for an invalid repeat count. Runtime identities were Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5. Local strict tracker health verifies history/storage integrity but reports an ambient pm-github extension-host skew (pinned host 2026.10.23 versus extension 2026.10.27); dependency pins are retained per task rules, and the clean CI health plus npm/Bun release gates will be the authoritative full-gate evidence in the PR. Public tracker version: digest:92fe4c9f9b66e74f154f9b3d7b8032cd035b02699906e29c04518352b4102034. All 83 public items were copied read-only outside git; both runtime validations preserve every file hash. No pm SDK defect is established by the transient orientation refusal: mismatched native focus answers fail safely and are not counted as passing samples."
  "2026-10-27T18:16:44.187Z",codex-agent,"Ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/167 (current checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/167/checks). Before final-head CI verification, added the missing registration regression that asserts starter baseline suppresses migration writes during preflight. Targeted registration/preflight selection passes 4 tests; the linked preflight selection passes 3 tests. Removing only the baseline preflight condition in a disposable copy fails the new test (true versus false); the actual source hash is unchanged and the fixed test passes after the revert probe. Initial queued CI run 40557212069 is superseded/canceled and is not approval evidence; fresh final-head npm/Bun gate URLs and counts are recorded in the PR. Automated review is unavailable: Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skips automatic review, Sourcery exceeds the diff-size limit. No review approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-27T18:38:10.142Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40558643711: Node 26 npm gate executed 204 tests, 203 passed and one SDK source-inventory test failed. All measured sources achieved 100% lines/branches/functions, including baselines.ts and index.ts; health, typecheck and committed-build verification passed. This is a missing first-release evidence row, not a measurement or coverage failure. Correcting the inventory against inert published artifacts and using a Pick of the native PmClient read methods so context/schemaList are also included in the source-derived inventory. The development SDK pin remains unchanged; host/peer minimum declarations will follow the actual published API boundary if it exceeds the prior floor."
  "2026-10-27T18:51:13.880Z",codex-agent,"SDK inventory repair verified: PmClient.context first 2026.7.6 (previous 2026.7.5), PmClient.schemaList first 2026.7.9 (previous 2026.7.8), ExtensionCommandSdk.isItemNotFoundError first 2026.7.24 (previous 2026.7.23). Exact positive/negative tarball hashes are committed in docs/sdk-floor.json and docs/sdk-floor.md; archives were inspected as data without executing their code or lifecycle scripts. All are below the existing 2026.8.18 API floor; no dependency or host-floor changes are needed. Native PmClient types now expose all used client methods to the source-derived inventory. The 7 SDK/floor tests pass, and the linked 10-test baseline suite again reaches 100% lines/branches/functions. Clone isolation is checked against a captured real SDK reply and native read-back; removing only the clone fails the shared-reference assertion in a disposable copy, and the fixed test passes after the probe. Repeated public-data validation again passes on Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5 with identical answers, unchanged hashes and the same 2/2/3-call, 5613/1643/6329-byte medians. Repacked acceptance passed all five install paths on exact artifact SHA-256 951cc2025ac7f1a745bef34ad5782768ed73caa176a38e109aee7291b0d78e20. Docstring gate passes with 103 documented declarations. Fresh exact-head npm/Bun CI gates remain required."
  "2026-10-27T18:59:28.109Z",codex-agent,"Final read-only transport verification: the native-typed facade exposes exactly context/get/list/listAllComplete/schemaList; create/update/delete and prototype/unknown properties are absent. The linked 10-test suite passes at 100% lines/branches/functions, and the 7 SDK/floor tests pass. Separate disposable-copy reverts of clone isolation and the read allowlist each fail the ownership/capability assertions; fixed source tests pass afterward. Final exact packed artifact is SHA-256 1bb25df3ced3bb796910b21d5c3be5ecaa990c566064bf8a9c4a24db42160824 (26 files, 80571 bytes); all five install paths pass identical-answer probes and typed refusals, including actual Bun through bunx. Both old Node 22/26 npm gates had 204 tests, 203 passes and only the now-repaired SDK-inventory failure; their 100% measured coverage is retained as diagnostic evidence, not final approval. Fresh current-head npm and Bun gates must pass before approval."
  "2026-10-27T19:42:04.206Z",codex-agent,"Re-review continuation: clean worktree at 14ad004; origin/main is not ahead (3 branch commits, 0 main-only commits), so no merge is needed. Reusing this item and PR 167. Blocking finding accepted: completion must be established by mutually consistent pagination signals, never by a null cursor alone. Class audit covers every package consumer of pagination/completeness metadata, both transports and all declare/run/probe and SDK/CLI rendering paths. Existing SDK-certified complete-list consumers do not implement cursor traversal; baseline resume is the sole manual traversal. Repair will also reject contradictory stop/continue flags, repeated cursors, duplicate or missing/foreign rows, and mismatch against the initial certified corpus rather than learning a partial expected answer. Existing compact continuation envelopes with omitted has_more remain supported."
  "2026-10-27T20:06:30.059Z",codex-agent,"Review fix class: a terminal marker alone cannot certify a traversal. Resume now requests strict SDK reads, validates mutually consistent cursor/flag/count/completeness receipts, and requires exact once-only coverage of the independently SDK-certified IDs and normalized statuses. Foreign, changed, duplicate or missing rows, cursor cycles and non-progress refuse before producing an answer. Package-wide audit found baseline resume is the only manual cursor traversal; other commands and laboratory/recipe SDK paths use native listAllComplete certification. JSON/TOON and directory/clone transports share this implementation. Previously released compact continuation envelopes remain allowed. No additional actionable non-blocking findings were supplied or posted inline. Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable package copy, replacing only runResume with its pre-fix body makes the two-item certified-corpus regression fail: the old function emits ok true with pages=1,rows=1 while corpus.item_count=2. Source worktree was never reverted. Fixed SDK tests passed; focused CLI tests passed for declare/run/probe in both output formats without Git. Added coverage for silent early termination as well. Test runners now cap workers at two without changing any coverage threshold."
  "2026-10-27T20:16:35.197Z",codex-agent,"Focused baseline suite: 14 tests passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled; baselines.ts reached 100% lines, branches and functions at unchanged thresholds. The linked two-item regression also passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress after the disposable revert proof. JSON/TOON CLI adversarial coverage now exercises both contradictory and silently short terminal pages in declare, run and probe with no Git executable. Read-only public corpus revalidation passed on Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5: 83 items, source hashes unchanged, identical expected answers. Calls/bytes are orientation 2/5613, targeted-read 2/1643, resume 3/6386. Strict native receipts add 57 resume bytes; the redundant full-list probe still adds exactly 1 call and 290014 bytes. Corpus digest remains 92fe4c9f9b66e74f154f9b3d7b8032cd035b02699906e29c04518352b4102034."
  "2026-10-27T20:24:28.876Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed for project-local, npm-global, Bun-global, npx and bunx forced through Bun: 5/5 consumers. Each reproduced all baseline answers, the deliberate waste probe and an invalid-input refusal; each also refused contradictory resume metadata in declare/run/probe in JSON and TOON (30 pagination refusals total). SDK always came from the host-injected context on a plain non-git tracker. Tested artifact SHA-256 5420d62c15aef76197eece8b1c192c96d2121097f0456ccc2eb92ee610086b7b; all 26 archive entries matched package files. The expanded cursor-bound/root-shape focused subset passed 2/2 tests. Full npm and Bun release checks now run sequentially with at most two workers and isolated identity/credential-free npm configuration."
  "2026-10-27T20:35:43.139Z",codex-agent,"The full npm coverage suite passed 208/208 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations. All six gate-scoped sources retain 100% lines, branches and functions; no thresholds changed. Existing native 500-sequence recipe state testing completed successfully. Release gate post-test audit, pack, changelog and publication-contract checks are finishing before the sequential Bun gate."
  "2026-10-27T20:48:04.389Z",codex-agent,"Review continuation complete locally: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed, sequentially, with at most two workers. Each ran 208 tests, all passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled; all six gate-scoped sources retained 100% lines, branches and functions. Typecheck, build, test typecheck, 104 documented declarations, production audit, pack, changelog and publication-contract checks passed. After both complete builds, every entry of the tested artifact still matches package files: SHA-256 5420d62c15aef76197eece8b1c192c96d2121097f0456ccc2eb92ee610086b7b, 26 files, 81711 compressed bytes. The supplied blocking finding is addressed as a pagination-completeness class with native SDK/CLI/packed/no-git regressions and a failing function-only behavioral revert. No additional actionable non-blocking findings were supplied or posted inline. Remote main remains unchanged; the prior three feature commits are retained. The final push will request fresh exact-head CI, whose run and counts will be linked in the PR. No merge or release is performed; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
